<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 06:20:21 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Africa</category><title>Nigerian president orders rescue operation after mass kidnapping in mosque</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260826-nigerian-president-tinubu-orders-rescue-operation-after-mass-kidnapping-in-mosque</link><description>
Nigerian President Bola Tinubu has ordered the military and other security agencies to launch an immediate rescue operation after the mass kidnapping of worshippers during an attack on a mosque in the north-central Niger State last week. While local authorities are still verifying the number abducted, local residents said about 600 women, children and elderly people were missing. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fba12020-32fd-11f0-a37e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-04-29T164615Z_786983510_RC2N5X9GBHUH_RTRMADP_3_NIGERIA-SECURITY-MILITARY.JPG"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fba12020-32fd-11f0-a37e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-04-29T164615Z_786983510_RC2N5X9GBHUH_RTRMADP_3_NIGERIA-SECURITY-MILITARY.JPG" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fd076dda-a114-11f1-8d4f-4d9d0ee435e5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 06:19:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fba12020-32fd-11f0-a37e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-04-29T164615Z_786983510_RC2N5X9GBHUH_RTRMADP_3_NIGERIA-SECURITY-MILITARY.JPG">REUTERS - Christophe Van der Perre</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Namibia to rebury remains of political prisoners returned by South Africa</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260826-namibia-to-rebury-remains-of-political-prisoners-returned-by-south-africa</link><description>
Two Namibian colonial-era political prisoners, whose remains were returned by South Africa last week, are to be reburied in Namibia as part of Wednesday’s Heroes Day ceremonies. They are among a group of Namibians who died in South Africa under apartheid or during the colonial period and whose remains have been repatriated.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bd65cd3e-12a5-11ea-9736-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2018-08-29t085135z_888509700_rc1fa2e0d7c0_rtrmadp_3_germany-namibia_0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bd65cd3e-12a5-11ea-9736-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2018-08-29t085135z_888509700_rc1fa2e0d7c0_rtrmadp_3_germany-namibia_0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83ec8b5a-9c9c-11f1-8280-f5365118855f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 04:55:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bd65cd3e-12a5-11ea-9736-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2018-08-29t085135z_888509700_rc1fa2e0d7c0_rtrmadp_3_germany-namibia_0.jpg">© Christian Mang/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>France says US risks ‘blocking everything’ at UN talks to protect world’s soils</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/environment/20260825-france-says-us-risks-blocking-everything-at-un-talks-to-protect-world-soils-cop17-desertification</link><description>
The soil that grows the world's food and holds its water is becoming less productive, yet governments are struggling to agree on how to respond to this crisis. As political talks at Cop17, the United Nations conference on desertification and land degradation, stepped up in Mongolia on Tuesday, France's environment ambassador Barbara Pompili warned that disputes involving the United States are threatening progress. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/25db6fc2-a098-11f1-a9d6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22305010588451.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/25db6fc2-a098-11f1-a9d6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22305010588451.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2868478e-a097-11f1-9bbb-23fdf51191ba</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 15:59:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/25db6fc2-a098-11f1-a9d6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22305010588451.jpg">AP - Rafiq Maqbool</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's Sophie Adenot returns to the void for second spacewalk in a week</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260825-french-astronaut-sophie-adenot-to-make-second-spacewalk-to-finish-repairs</link><description>
French astronaut Sophie Adenot on Tuesday stepped outside the International Space Station (ISS) for the second time, a week after she became the first French woman to perform a spacewalk. Adenot and US astronaut Anil Menon are due to finish replacing a faulty antenna on the ISS after running out of time during their first spacewalk on 18 August.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c386df8a-9fc2-11f1-b73a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-18T193750Z-1637559858-RC211NAFX3V1-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEWALK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c386df8a-9fc2-11f1-b73a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-18T193750Z-1637559858-RC211NAFX3V1-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEWALK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d50039fa-9fc2-11f1-b33b-e347e9354ddc</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 05:57:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c386df8a-9fc2-11f1-b73a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-18T193750Z-1637559858-RC211NAFX3V1-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEWALK.jpg">via REUTERS - NASA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Looking up: French radio enthusiast captures ISS signals from his garage</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260825-looking-up-french-radio-enthusiast-captures-iss-signals-from-his-garage</link><description>
Astronaut Sophie Adenot made history this month as the first French woman to perform a spacewalk. Back on Earth, space enthusiasts across France are finding their own ways to reach for the stars. In the second episode of a five-part series, RFI hears from Vincent Plousey, a radio ham from Tavaux in eastern France whose hobby is picking up signals from the ISS using homemade antennas built in his garage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/47b9e1ae-9fc2-11f1-8cd5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/DSC-0284.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/47b9e1ae-9fc2-11f1-8cd5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/DSC-0284.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8dd209ca-9fc0-11f1-b750-e347e9354ddc</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 13:48:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/47b9e1ae-9fc2-11f1-8cd5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/DSC-0284.jpg">© Baptiste Coulon / RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Survivors of Guinea's deadly landfill collapse say authorities ignored warnings</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260825-survivors-of-guinea-s-deadly-landfill-collapse-say-authorities-ignored-warnings</link><description>
Two days after a deadly landfill collapse in Guinea, rescuers are using giant excavators to search for victims. Anger is rising among residents, who say they had warned authorities that the rubbish dump was precarious.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7284eb0e-9f36-11f1-b23d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6BN4GG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7284eb0e-9f36-11f1-b23d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6BN4GG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4c158146-a06b-11f1-a6a2-f1db79bccd1e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 12:10:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7284eb0e-9f36-11f1-b23d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6BN4GG.jpg">AFP - -</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>US and Denmark push for nationwide expansion of UN arms embargo in Sudan</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260825-us-and-denmark-push-for-nationwide-expansion-of-un-arms-embargo-in-sudan</link><description>
The United States on Monday urged the United Nations Security Council to expand an arms embargo on the Sudanese region of Darfur to cover all of Sudan, saying the nation's brutal conflict risks regional expansion. The suggestion was supported by Denmark, which holds the Council's rotating presidency. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/09831f54-2d95-11f0-9636-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25123519167407.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/09831f54-2d95-11f0-9636-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25123519167407.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d45c51f4-a081-11f1-a5dd-bfda8eb3ae4b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 15:00:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/09831f54-2d95-11f0-9636-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25123519167407.jpg">© AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>At least 40 killed as gangs attack displaced people near Haiti capital</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260825-at-least-40-killed-as-gangs-attack-displaced-people-near-haiti-capital</link><description>
At least 40 people have been killed, some execution-style, after gangs attacked displaced people sheltering in a church near Haiti's capital Port-au-Prince at the weekend, local authorities said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dd5c43a8-a019-11f1-aa1f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236704099772.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dd5c43a8-a019-11f1-aa1f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236704099772.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8485013a-a059-11f1-9823-679e8866c115</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 08:53:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dd5c43a8-a019-11f1-aa1f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236704099772.jpg">© AP Photo/Odelyn Joseph</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French village reels from tornado that damaged hundreds of homes</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260825-french-village-reels-from-tornado-that-damaged-hundreds-of-homes</link><description>
Hundreds of damaged homes, widespread power cuts and blocked roads confronted residents of southwestern France on Tuesday after a tornado tore through the village of Pomas, injuring 39 people, two of them critically.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4d47dd7a-a052-11f1-9f0c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6F74ZQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4d47dd7a-a052-11f1-9f0c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6F74ZQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4d36d51c-a04c-11f1-93b2-dd9b3ccbcf49</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 09:59:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4d47dd7a-a052-11f1-9f0c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6F74ZQ.jpg">AFP - CYRILLE KALDOR / UGC / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Namibia paves way for phosphate mining in the Atlantic Ocean</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260825-namibia-paves-way-for-phosphate-mining-in-the-atlantic-ocean</link><description>
Namibia has granted environmental clearance for an offshore phosphate mining project that paves the way for the world's first commercial seabed-dredging operation for the mineral, despite opposition from green groups and the fishing industry.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/51fdb99a-a046-11f1-bb8a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ed9e94009377e5e8e0ade5ed52204e6e27aa4874.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/51fdb99a-a046-11f1-bb8a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ed9e94009377e5e8e0ade5ed52204e6e27aa4874.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">52cbf148-a046-11f1-bc5f-2b4787bb34a0</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 05:32:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/51fdb99a-a046-11f1-bb8a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ed9e94009377e5e8e0ade5ed52204e6e27aa4874.jpg">© MARCO LONGARI / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Ukraine's allies pledge to continue support with focus on air defence</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260824-ukraine-s-allies-pledge-to-continue-support-with-focus-on-air-defence</link><description>
Ukraine's allies on Monday pledged to keep up their support in the war against Russia, with a renewed focus on air defence investment to counter a shortage of US Patriot interceptors. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/71afd38c-9fa5-11f1-af79-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236363361580.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/71afd38c-9fa5-11f1-af79-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236363361580.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f9103d0e-9fe5-11f1-8ca1-af870d26e276</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 19:17:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/71afd38c-9fa5-11f1-af79-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236363361580.jpg">© Henry Nicholls / Pool AFP via AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Saudi Arabia to invest €6bn in building theme parks near Paris</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260824-saudi-arabia-to-invest-7-bn-in-theme-parks-near-paris-french-presidency</link><description>
France and Saudi Arabia on Monday signed a memo of understanding for a €6 billion Saudi investment to create three theme parks near Paris, the office of the French president said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c4cc18b4-9fe6-11f1-bfdc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/e5bef9e73595ec0265cbf9aa320acbe08d2c098a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c4cc18b4-9fe6-11f1-bfdc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/e5bef9e73595ec0265cbf9aa320acbe08d2c098a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c5e83b10-9fe6-11f1-a438-af870d26e276</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 18:08:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c4cc18b4-9fe6-11f1-bfdc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/e5bef9e73595ec0265cbf9aa320acbe08d2c098a.jpg">© LOU BENOIST / POOL/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Mediterranean migrant rescue ships threatened by Libyan groups, warns NGO</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260824-mediterranean-migrant-rescue-ships-threatened-by-libyan-groups-warns-ngo</link><description>
A leading group monitoring and providing aid to migrants crossing the Mediterranean have warned that its rescue ships have been facing increasing threats and harassment from Libyan groups.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/148ae9a0-8059-11f1-9930-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-92ZB9ZR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/148ae9a0-8059-11f1-9930-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-92ZB9ZR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a4727752-9fa5-11f1-a762-d969d98d7dd8</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 12:22:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/148ae9a0-8059-11f1-9930-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-92ZB9ZR.jpg">© Sameer al-Doumy/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Malian PM's visit to Algeria underlines need for mutual security goals</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260824-malian-pm-s-visit-to-algeria-underlines-need-for-mutual-security-goals</link><description>
The acting head of the Malian government, General Abdoulaye Maiga has begun a two-day visit to Algeria. It comes amid a thaw after months of tension. RFI spoke to Bakary Sambe, the Director of the Timbuktu Institute about the security situation and what the countries hope to gain from the meeting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/626a8dea-9fc3-11f1-aa7c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22312578792228-Abdoulaye-Ma%C3%AFga.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/626a8dea-9fc3-11f1-aa7c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22312578792228-Abdoulaye-Ma%C3%AFga.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83603542-9fc1-11f1-8b4e-e347e9354ddc</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 15:25:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/626a8dea-9fc3-11f1-aa7c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22312578792228-Abdoulaye-Ma%C3%AFga.jpg">AP - Peter Dejong</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Six million Somalis face acute hunger as drought and conflict worsen</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260824-six-million-somalis-face-acute-hunger-as-drought-and-conflict-worsen</link><description>
Six million people in Somalia are facing acute hunger, with nearly two million children at emergency levels, as severe drought, conflict and falling humanitarian funding deepen what the UN describes as one of the world’s worst malnutrition crises. Medical charity MSF tells RFI it's sounding the alarm "before it's too late".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/089fa040-9f80-11f1-979d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26232458355606-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/089fa040-9f80-11f1-979d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26232458355606-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e9ca8582-9f97-11f1-9ee8-75486ab540dd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 10:40:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/089fa040-9f80-11f1-979d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26232458355606-1.jpg">©  Farah Abdi Warsameh / AP Photo</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Violence against healthcare workers in DRC hampers Ebola response</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260824-violence-against-healthcare-workers-in-drc-hampers-ebola-response</link><description>
Healthcare workers in the Democratic Republic of Congo have been coming under attack, the United Nations and Red Cross have warned, hampering efforts to stem the spread of the Ebola virus, which is spreading 'exponentially'.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7a5c8358-9d67-11f1-b9dd-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-31T085519Z-246925543-RC23HLAKM9NK-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7a5c8358-9d67-11f1-b9dd-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-31T085519Z-246925543-RC23HLAKM9NK-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cd402608-9f9f-11f1-896c-8324a3ed262e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 10:08:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7a5c8358-9d67-11f1-b9dd-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-31T085519Z-246925543-RC23HLAKM9NK-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA.jpg">© Gradel Muyisa Mumbere/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Centre-left Glucksmann enters French presidential race as left tries to unite</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260824-centre-left-glucksmann-enters-french-presidential-race-as-left-tries-to-unite</link><description>
French centre-left politician Raphael Glucksmann has announced his candidacy for next year's presidential election, seeking to challenge hard-left leader Jean-Luc Melenchon to lead France's fractured left, as a campaign increasingly dominated by the far right takes shape.
